~ start
if check_perfect() == true && first == true:
	=>< Perfect
	set first = false
	=> END
elif first == true:
	=>< Introduction
	set first = false
	=> END
else:
	=>< Reintroduction
	=> END


~ Perfect
The Old Man: Ah, yet another shining face has made it. So many more today than usual.
The Old Man: Is that your doing? It brings my heart so much warmth.
The Old Man: Your friends are waiting for you above.
The Old Man: Still, your wings may not have the strength to make it up that cliff. 
The Old Man: Here, I want you to have this. I’ve been saving it for just such an occasion.
do give_feathers()
The Old Man: Still, if you lack the courage to make the final leap, you may rest here as long as you like.
 => END

~ Introduction
The Old Man: Ah, another aspiring prisoner
The Old Man: Congratulations are in order! Enjoy the feeling of the sun and the breeze.
The Old Man: Do you see that cliff? If you truly desire freedom, then you must make one final climb. 
The Old Man: I have seen many try to reach the top, and nearly as many fail. I myself never had the courage for that final leap.
The Old Man: So, here I sit. 
The Old Man: You may rest here as well, if you like.
 => END

~ Reintroduction
The Old Man: Doesn’t the breeze feel nice? The air is so soothing out here.
 => END
